  "body": "Qualifies the additive social migrations against the repository's complete schema fixture, where real column types, constraints and 102 registered migrations supplement the earlier minimal social fixtures. It checks repeated application, publication backfill and original post writes, block denial, and pause that preserves every new command/publication snapshot.\n\nDepends on #367 and the preceding stack. Tests/CI/docs only; keep draft and unmerged. No runtime flag or production migration is activated. The branch inherits provider suppression and uses the Cloudflare-specific skip prefix without disabling CI.\n\nActual evidence: private native PostgreSQL 16.10 with pgvector passed twice, including the final portable harness; all reconciliation violations were zero. Twelve workflow guard tests passed. The private pgvector/pgvector:pg17 CI job passed the complete schema step at b689f88e2 (run 34991068129). Existing social model/client CI at parent 9a68db744 passed; the refreshed Stack-linked backend test binary passed 2,542 examples with zero failures; the separate executable compilation and broader backend CI remain independently tracked.\n\nRun `TDF_SOCIAL_SCHEMA_NATIVE=1 bash scripts/social/test-schema-compatibility.sh` for installed PostgreSQL, or `bash scripts/social/test-schema-compatibility.sh` for Docker. The script accepts no existing database URL and only creates its own fixture. Detailed commands, results and limits are in docs/social/schema-compatibility.md.\n\nThis is schema-fixture qualification, not live-data migration, concurrent production index-lock measurement, or old/new application coexistence. Legacy DM/media/notification block bypasses still prevent activation. Roll back this test-only PR by reverting it; the prior preserved-data pause remains the application rollback policy. Do not remove new block/consent/publication records or route activated users to a legacy binary that ignores them.\n\n\n## Parent reconciliation \u2014 2026-09-16\n\nNormal merge `3606fb5c2215e00b1f3661abdf9e969231ac3b36` preserves original head `64fa01f19e6a9a65e5e177f904e86fd9f80ea8cf` and current parent `0bac512baed505f7f035f44c022fc0b64405b9e7`. No shared history was rewritten. Social runtime, SQL, models, tests and social workflow remain byte-identical to the original head. Previously merged artwork and Instagram changes from the parent remain intact; catalog outputs were regenerated with the unchanged strict policy.\n\nVerified locally on the reconciled tree: complete schema PostgreSQL fixture and all registered migrations, additive reapplication, legacy writes and pause preservation; repository quality; strict catalog JSON and CSV (1,420 scanned files, 1,114 reviewed candidates). All exited 0. No test or security gate was weakened.\n\nNew exact-head hosted checks and any renewed review remain required. Existing feature and migration activation gates are unchanged. No manual deployment was performed. Native-stack integration remains separately blocked by its linear-history requirement; this update does not claim the stack is merged.\n",
